# Gaining Algorithmic Insight through Simplifying Constraints.

**Authors:** Ginat, David

## Abstract
Discusses algorithmic problem solving in computer science education, particularly algorithmic insight, and focuses on the relevance and effectiveness of the heuristic simplifying constraints which involves simplification of a given problem to a problem in which constraints are imposed on the input data. Presents three examples involving mathematical formulation, spatial calculations, and optimization. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ656047

